    "source": "CityTop",
    "art": {
      "style": "Moody nighttime cityscape painting with photographic realism softened into painterly strokes. Near-black sky, dark charcoal and brown building masses punctuated by thousands of warm amber window lights, with occasional cool blue accents. Lighting comes from below and from windows, rims of warm gold on edges, deep shadows elsewhere.",
      "reference": "stages/city-top/reference.webp"
    },
    "notes": "Plays like a standard three-platform stage on a wide rooftop: billboard catwalk and skylight canopy at 140, water tower lid at 280 for vertical play. The right side has a two-landing fire escape below roof level that catches fighters knocked off that side, giving them a climb-back route (lower landing reaches the ledge with a full jump plus air jump); the left side is an open drop, so the stage is mildly asymmetric by design. Every KO launches a firework into the sky; the match end fires a big multicolor finale. Art priority: main-building, water-tower, fire-escape, billboard-catwalk, skylight-canopy, backdrop, escape-building, front-antenna, left-building."
  }
